// Repro from a plain clone (golden case for TestSanitizeIntegration):
//
//	git clone https://github.com/gnolang/gno && cd gno
//	git fetch origin pull/6304/head && git checkout a8bdd53b08e988227136f8b74f4cd6571956e5f4
//	cp <this file> gno.land/pkg/gnoweb/markdown/golden/sanitize/
//	go test ./gno.land/pkg/gnoweb/markdown -run 'TestSanitizeIntegration/b3-lines-removed-reach-catalog-block-pipeless-table' -count=1 -v
//
// Strict sanitize.Block promises user content cannot inject "GFM table rows"
// and stays paragraph-shaped, but escapeLineLeader only escapes a
// line-LEADING `|`. GFM tables need no leading pipe, so a header line and a
// `--- | ---` delimiter row (neither a thematic break, a list marker nor a
// setext underline) render a live <table> through Block. Predates this PR:
// the merge base escapes only a line-leading `|` too.
//
// Sections below pin the head's actual output (the test passes at head).
// Fixed expectation: output.html is paragraph text, no <table>.
// MARKDOWNFUNC: Block
// CONTEXT: REALM BEFORE\n%s\nREALM AFTER
-- input.md --
a | b
--- | ---
c | d
-- output.md --


a | b
--- | ---
c | d

-- output.html --
<p>REALM BEFORE</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>a</th>
<th>b</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>c</td>
<td>d</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>REALM AFTER</p>
